<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul to buy soybean from Continental, Tradigrain.</title>
<headline>Seoul to buy soybean from Continental, Tradigrain.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Agricultural and Fishery Marketing Corp (AFMC) said on Friday it would buy 20,000 tonnes of No.1 soybean from Continental and another 20,000 tonnes from Tradigrain.  </p>
<p>The corporation held a tender earlier today and picked the two U.S. companies as suppliers.</p>
<p>Results of the tender are as follow:</p>
<p> POSITION TONNE   SUPPLIER	  SHIPMENT	  ARRIVAL/PORT</p>
<p>					  U.S. GULF</p>
<p>  ONE    20,000  Continental   May 26-Jun 15    Jul 20/Inchon</p>
<p>  TWO    20,000  Tradigrain    Jun 26-Jul 15    Aug 20'Inchon</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
